//! Port of wal.c.
//!
//! Skeleton generated by gen_skel.py: every `todo!()` is a function
//! still to be ported.  See PORTING.md.
//!
//! WAL mode is not supported yet: the unix VFS has no shared memory and
//! sqlite3PagerWalSupported() returns 0, so the pager never opens a Wal
//! (Pager::pWal stays None) and none of these stubs is ever called.  The
//! signatures were adapted to the pager port (page lists are slices,
//! callbacks are closures, the busy handler is the pager's Rc closure).

#![allow(unused_variables, unused_mut, dead_code, unused_imports)]

